### Signup user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "post-file-create@example.com",
  "password": "password1234",
  "nickname": "postFileCreateUser"
}


### Login user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "post-file-create@example.com",
  "password": "password1234"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.data.accessToken);
%}


### Create post - multipart success with png
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=post-create-boundary

--post-create-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="categoryId"

1
--post-create-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Spring multipart question
--post-create-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="content"

Post content with an attached file.
--post-create-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="question.png"
Content-Type: image/png

fake-png-content
--post-create-boundary--

> {%
    client.global.set("postId", response.body.data.postId);
%}


### Create post - invalid file type
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=post-invalid-type-boundary

--post-invalid-type-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="categoryId"

1
--post-invalid-type-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Invalid file type
--post-invalid-type-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="content"

Only images and PDFs are allowed.
--post-invalid-type-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="memo.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

text file content
--post-invalid-type-boundary--


### Create post - empty file
POST http://localhost:8080/api/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=post-empty-file-boundary

--post-empty-file-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="categoryId"

1
--post-empty-file-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Empty file
--post-empty-file-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="content"

Empty files are rejected.
--post-empty-file-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="empty.png"
Content-Type: image/png

--post-empty-file-boundary--


